        "content": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>Last year, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"543250\">@SnO2WMaN</span> and I launched a formalization project, <a href=\"https://github.com/FormalizedFormalLogic\">FormalizedFormalLogic</a>, aiming to formalize various results in formal logic.</p>\n<p>The current results and progress are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Classical Propositional Logic<ul>\n<li>completeness theorem.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>(Minimal/Intuitionistic/Superintuitionistic) Propositional Logic<ul>\n<li>Kripke completeness.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Classical First-Order Logic and Arithmetic<ul>\n<li>compactness theorem.</li>\n<li>completeness theorem.</li>\n<li>cut elimination.</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-completeness of theories stronger than <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">R</mi><mn mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{R_0}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3089em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathsf mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Gödel's first and second incompleteness theorems.<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/G.C3.B6del's.20Incompleteness.20Theorem\">thread</a></li>\n<li>FYI: These theorems have been formalized many times, but my results are stronger.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>WIP:</strong> ordinal analysis of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{PA}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">PA</span></span></span></span></span>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>(Minimal/Intuitionistic/Superintuitionistic) First-Order Logic:<ul>\n<li>Gödel-Gentzen translation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Modal Logic<ul>\n<li>Kripke completenes of Geach modal logics (e.g. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathsf\">K</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">S</mi><mn mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{S4}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">S4</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">S</mi><mn mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{S5}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">S5</span></span></span></span></span>).</li>\n<li>Kripke completeness (finite frame property) of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{GL}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">GL</span></span></span></span></span><ul>\n<li>FYI: This result is already formalized in HOL Light by <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-023-09677-z\">Maggesi &amp; Brogi 2023</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Gödel-McKinsey-Tarski theorem (Modal logic <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">S</mi><mn mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{S4}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">S4</span></span></span></span></span> and intuitionistic propositional logic can be interpretable each other via Gödel translation), proved by using Kripke semantics.</li>\n<li><strong>WIP:</strong> Solovay's arithmetical completeness of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"sans-serif\">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{GL}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathsf\">GL</span></span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li><strong>WIP:</strong> Negri's labelled sequent caliculi for modal logic.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Basically, the fundamentals and classical logics were developed by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"414485\">@Palalansoukî</span>, while non-classical logics were handled by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"543250\">@SnO2WMaN</span>.</p>\n<p>Collaborators are welcome! Many areas—such as the algebraic semantics of modal logic, intermediate logic, and non-standard modal logics (e.g., Hybrid Logic, Relevant Logic, etc.)—have not yet been addressed. If you are interested, please ask us.</p>",
        "id": 491989654,
